From: Phil <300208363+calicopizzadelivery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:18:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add screensaver, accessibility and audio output tiles to
 the panel

The system options panel carried network, accessories and the power actions.
These three are the ones a TV box is actually asked for mid-session, and all
three report state rather than just linking to a settings screen, so the panel
is worth opening even when nothing needs changing.

Audio output reads the live output from AudioManager rather than listing what
is attached, ordered by what overrides what: a connected A2DP sink or wired
headphones take audio away from HDMI, and HDMI takes it from the built-in
speaker. It opens DisplaySoundActivity, which advertises
com.android.settings.SOUND_SETTINGS.

Screensaver surfaces something easy to miss: screensaver_enabled is 1 out of
the box while screensaver_components is unset, so the screensaver looks on and
has nothing to show. The tile says "Not set" in that state. It opens
DaydreamActivity by explicit name, since that activity is exported but carries
no intent filter, and ACTION_DREAM_SETTINGS resolves to nothing on TV.

Accessibility reports how many services are actually running rather than
simply linking to the screen, because "no services on" is the common case on a
TV box and is worth seeing at a glance.

Laid out two per row alongside the existing tiles.

Verified on lineage_sdk_tv_x86_64: all three render with live state, and both
new intents resolve and launch.

